WEBVTT

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.110
<b>I ♥ Aoyama</b>

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.110
Team 
Aoyama

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.300
Damn it!

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.430
Clean! Clean! A-o-ya-ma!

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:18.790
Clean! Clean! A-o-ya-ma!

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:21.420
C-Captain, what are you doing?

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:33.720
Clean! Clean! A-o-ya-ma!

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.180
Nice shot! Good job, Aoyama!

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.490
Th-Thanks.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:33.550
<i>I never expected our captain to join 
Aoyama's fan club: Team Aoyama.</i>

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.250
Oh.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.180
Here it comes!

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.770
There, there, there, there!

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:40.760
And there it is!

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.520
The time-honored treasure in
four eyes' arsenal, butt keepie-uppie!

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:45.400
There, there, there, there!

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.540
<i>It's working! It's working!</i>

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.310
<i>This'll work tomorrow, too.</i>

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:54.450
<i>I'm all about scoring laughs, not goals!</i>

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.000
<b>#05</b>

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.000
<b>Tsukamoto-kun's Life Is
All About Laughs</b>

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.150
Gotcha!

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:33.770
Four eyes!

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:35.810
Yeah!

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.800
The three stooges are combining nicely.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.540
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.010
Go!

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:47.680
Oops!

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.090
Hey!

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.020
Um...

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:50.700
Hi-yah!

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:53.430
Ow!

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.790
You're taking it too far.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:00.100
But it's great that you put 
the team in a good mood.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.040
Do the same in tomorrow's match, too.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.280
Leave it to me.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:05.310
Go!

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.120
There!

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:06.760
Go!

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:07.580
There!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.390
Go!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.880
You're goofing off too much!

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.570
It's fine. Tsukamoto's our
"good vibes" officer.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:22.010
This is just another day for him.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.460
Another!

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:24.840
Oops.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.890
Dodge! Dodge! Dodge! Dodge! Dodge!

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.130
He dodged it! Aoyama dodged it!

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:42.450
He dodged it! Aoyama dodged it!

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.450
Captain, what are you doing?!

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.590
You didn't know, Zaizen?
His girlfriend's an Aoyama fan.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:50.470
I've gained a newfound respect
for our captain.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:54.030
Gaku-kun...

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:55.710
Yurippe...

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:59.320
Good luck!

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.320
Thanks!

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:02.470
Yuri—

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:09.770
<b>I ♥
Aoyama</b>

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:08.140
I only love you, Gaku.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:12.730
<b>I ♥
Aoyama</b>

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:22.740
I didn't think he'd choose the life of 
being an Aoyama fan with his girlfriend.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.100
I see.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:29.080
He's a member of the Aoyama fan club
<i>and</i> the soccer team captain.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.660
I'll get going now.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.250
Yeah, do your best!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:39.000
<b>Curse</b>

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.040
<i>This team is rotten to the core.</i>

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:44.720
Good morning!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.470
Yes, good morni—

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.890
A-o-ya-ma! A-o-ya-ma!

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.400
A-o-ya-ma! A-o-ya-ma!

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:07.990
A-o-ya-ma! A-o-ya-ma!

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.080
I totally didn't eat enough yesterday.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.010
Are you kidding me?

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:02.780
Feed us our post-match meal again.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:03.860
My treat again?

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.090
Get lost!

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:14.230
I never thought the day would come
when the statue wouldn't be useless.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:23.330
Today's field is grass! Woo!

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.500
Random diving!

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.720
We didn't come here to fool around!

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.630
I-I don't see Aoyama-kun anywhere!

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.670
Not again!

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:33.720
Hi.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.910
Damn you! Where have you been?!

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:39.320
A-o-ya-ma! A-o-ya-ma!

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.490
A-o-ya-ma! A-o-ya-ma!

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.230
A-o-ya-ma! A-o-ya-ma!

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.030
I'm going now, Yurippe.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.200
Okay. Good luck, Gaku.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:51.790
Gather round!

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:54.870
Hell no! What's wrong with you?!

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.790
Four eyes! Do that thing you always do!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.730
Y-Yeah, I got it!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.300
It's what we've all been waiting for!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:06.720
Ow!

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:11.810
I'm sorry! My ball flew over this way!

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.170
Are you okay?

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:20.980
Hi, I'm the captain of Minamida Fuzoku
High School, Kadomatsu Ryou.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:29.950
Nice to meet you.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.300
What's wrong, four eyes? You've gone pale.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.750
Have you got a stomachache?

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.830
What? Haha, no, I'm fine!

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.790
Let's go warm up!

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.180
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.180
<b>1st</b>

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.180
<b>2nd</b>

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.180
<b>Total</b>

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.180
<b>Minamida Fuzoku</b>

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.890
Don't let him through!
Force him to the wings!

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:55.900
Here it comes!

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:04.730
Aoyama's really something.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:07.770
He's playing on a whole other level.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:14.180
You know, in the high school soccer world,

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:18.080
Fujimi High School may very well 
become the eye of the storm.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:19.880
I don't know about that.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:23.450
I've shot high school soccer
for 20 years now.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:29.010
And Aoyama, with his exceptional talent,
is certainly the real deal.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:32.300
But that's what's so damning.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:36.190
This isn't the kind of team
he should be playing for.

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:37.710
As long as they win, it's all good.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:40.930
But what happens if they lose 
a preliminary match like this?

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.130
In this game, results are everything.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:48.400
You may have a world-beater,
 but if the team loses, that's it.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.740
Even a player like Aoyama won't get picked 
for the national team if they lose so early.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:56.280
And then, he won't have any choice 
but to leave Fujimi High School.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:01.250
If this team wants to keep their dream alive,
they must keep winning for him.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:06.200
However, high school soccer crushes
thousands of similar dreams every year.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.240
It's no walk in the park.

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:08.670
Shige, pass it!

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:10.290
Gotcha!

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:14.110
<i>This team only has Aoyama going for it.</i>

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:16.890
<i>In my eyes, this team has a major weakness.</i>

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.060
<i>And that weakness...</i>

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.520
Don't give him any space, four eyes!

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.690
<i>...is you.</i>

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:39.490
What? He got into the box with ease!

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:48.370
All right!

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:50.090
Nice pass, Kadomatsu!

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:52.130
Now, we're tied!

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:56.090
What are you doing?! 
Stop sleepwalking and play!

00:08:58.290 --> 00:08:59.220
Sorry...

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.320
Anyway, we're still in the first half.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:05.520
L-Let's get back into the game.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:23.120
Down the right wing again?
This time, he put it in himself!

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:25.170
Hey, four eyes!

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:29.140
Same old, same old, huh, Tsukamoto?

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.010
You haven't changed 
one bit since the old days.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.970
You really are just a statue.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.010
<i>Did something happen between them?</i>

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.320
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.320
<b>1st</b>

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.320
<b>2nd</b>

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.320
<b>Total</b>

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.320
<b>Minamida Fuzoku</b>

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:59.630
I guess the first half's ending 2-1.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:05.750
Minamida Fuzoku's parked the bus
ever since they took the lead.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:09.060
But yeah, looking at Fujimi High School...

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.460
Their number 4 has destroyed their game plan.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:13.830
Captain, where's four eyes?

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:17.170
He walked off toward the school,
 so maybe he went to the bathroom?

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:39.510
Dammit.

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:45.870
Aoyama's something else, but it looks 
like we've got the better of Fujimi.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.910
Thanks to that specky slow-mo.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:55.500
I heard their number 4 was in the same team
as Kadomatsu-san in middle school.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.890
I heard that, too.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.520
He used to act all high and mighty
despite being younger,

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:02.340
so he got bullied constantly 
until he graduated, right?

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:06.110
So that's why he's still terrified
of Kadomatsu-san.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:11.270
Otherwise, he wouldn't be 
such a liability in defense.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:14.120
Well, after screwing up that much,

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.750
he probably won't play the second half.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:25.820
Man, that idiot. Why didn't he tell us?

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:26.770
Right?

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:32.620
<i>I need to get going,
or the second half will start without me.</i>

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:39.400
Whoa! Aoyama, you were in here, too?!

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:42.050
Don't tell me you've been here
the whole time...

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:45.850
You use too much paper.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.480
<i>That's</i> the main talking point for you?!

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:49.020
Wait, that means you heard everything!

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:51.180
Not that it matters.

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:57.340
I won't be playing the second half, anyway.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:01.030
Tsukamoto-san.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:03.500
What?

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:08.080
<b>Team Aoyama Member and 
Soccer Team Captain!</b>

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:08.080
<b>Ishikawa Gaku</b>

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:08.080
<b>Tamura Yuri</b>

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:11.080
<b>Thinks too highly
 of himself!</b>

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:11.080
<b>Kadomatsu 
Ryou</b>

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:14.040
The second half is starting!

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:24.930
<i>Why didn't you sub me out, Miwa-chan?</i>

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:32.510
<i>It's true that you're currently 
a burden on the team, but...</i>

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:38.020
Miwa-chan... No, Coach...

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:42.820
You can sub him out immediately
if we concede another goal from his wing,

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:46.030
but can you please keep four eyes 
on the field for a bit longer?

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:49.320
Please!

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:57.290
<i>Those two goof-offs always mess around,
but they asked me so seriously.</i>

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.210
<i>I can't help but want to trust them.</i>

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:02.540
<i>Now's the time for you to fight, Tsukamoto.</i>

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:07.140
<i>For your friends. And for yourself.</i>

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:11.270
Why didn't Fujimi sub out the number 4?

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:12.340
Beats me.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:14.100
What I do know is that,

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.560
as long as he's out there,

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:23.120
he'll keep being targeted 
by the other team.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:24.870
Another attack down the right wing!

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.410
<i>Tsukamoto.</i>

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.940
That's amazing, Tsukamoto!

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:45.820
You're not that good at soccer... 
How come you can do stuff like that?

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:47.300
That's so funny!

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.100
Talk about annoying.

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:04.160
What's the point of performing
keepie-uppies with your butt?

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.070
Are you stupid?

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.580
It's annoying, so never do it again.

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.940
Come on, guys. It's time for practice.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.850
<i>Kadomatsu-san was a second-year,
and as the star player,</i>

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:19.940
<i>he was the center of the team.</i>

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:22.940
<i>Ever since that day,
whenever I drew attention to myself,</i>

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:25.010
<i>he'd fire a ball at me.</i>

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:27.770
<i>After that happened a few times,</i>

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:33.970
<i>I began to freeze up in front of him,
unable to move.</i>

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:38.420
You're so freaking boring. 
You're like a statue.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.980
<i>Guys, I'm sorry for being such a burden.</i>

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:46.920
<i>It's like I've traveled back in time!</i>

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.400
<i>I can't move!</i>

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.640
Their number 4 let him run past 
like he wasn't there again!

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.830
Not on my watch!

00:14:56.790 --> 00:15:00.250
<i>If we know you're gonna ghost
past him every time, we can stop you!</i>

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.170
Nice, Sakai!

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.780
Don't let him go through you so easily.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:09.530
I'll cover you, so be more aggressive.

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:13.210
<i>Sakai, I'm sorry.</i>

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.710
Get your head in the game, four eyes.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.650
You're Fujimi High School's
"good vibes" officer, after all.

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.220
Take it!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:39.200
Shouldn't Aoyama be able 
to create more chances?

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:42.170
It's probably difficult right now.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:45.780
Minamida Fuzoku is keeping 
more players behind the ball.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:50.080
But, and I don't know how to explain this,

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.660
it feels like he's waiting for something.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.210
At least, it does to me.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:16:01.000
Either way, if they don't
make something happen,

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.980
Fujimi High School will lose.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.940
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.940
<b>1st</b>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.940
<b>2nd</b>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.940
<b>Total</b>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.940
<b>Minamida Fuzoku</b>

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.010
Here of all places.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.280
Ten minutes left.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.700
They're going down the right again!

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.760
<i>Dammit! Move!</i>

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:20.290
<i>You coward!</i>

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.250
I won't let you!

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:35.000
Yocchi!

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.300
Sub out number 4!

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:40.470
He's useless!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:41.930
Shut up!

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:46.830
Listen up, four eyes!
You have me and Yocchi behind you!

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:49.110
We can't get going without you.

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:51.120
So stop running away!

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:54.060
Don't you realize
you're turning into a total bore?

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.470
Sakai. Yocchi.

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.580
<i>When I joined the soccer team here,</i>

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.970
<i>I was still depressed.</i>

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:12.920
You're so funny, Yoshioka!

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:15.880
Coming your way!

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:24.810
<i>But thanks to you, I was able to
have fun playing soccer again.</i>

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:35.890
<i>I'm no longer...</i>

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:41.660
They're holding on, but Fujimi 
can't get out of their own half!

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.170
I won't let you shoot!

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.450
It was a feint!

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:49.580
Crap! Kadomatsu's free!

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:53.550
<i>A statue? Piss off.</i>

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.260
<i>That's...</i>

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.580
...so freaking boring!

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:03.180
I'm not the old me anymore!

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:05.140
Four eyes!

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:10.950
Bastard!

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.640
Nice, Tsukamoto!

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:14.530
Aoyama!

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:19.310
Let's go! Time to counterattack!

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:23.290
Aoyama's heading down the right!

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.410
Is he going to cross it?

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:27.070
Who's the target?

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.340
<i>I'm ready anytime, Aoyama!</i>

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.300
Huh? He's not passing?

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:37.620
No! He waited too long, 
and now he's surrounded!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:41.720
Are you really going to lose here?

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:46.190
Aoyama!

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:49.140
Their number 4's making an overlapping run?!

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:58.070
In the second half, try to come forward
when you spot the chance.

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:00.610
No, like I just said...

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:05.290
I'm going to send a pass out to you.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:11.350
<i>Aoyama...</i>

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.210
A rabona!

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:20.960
<i>What am I supposed to do with this pass?!</i>

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:24.550
<i>Should I use my foot?
No, it's definitely at head height.</i>

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:26.090
<i>You idiot!</i>

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:29.020
<i>I don't have the skills 
to deal with this cross!</i>

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:31.480
Tsukamoto-san.

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:35.440
Please do that thing 
you do to lift our spirits.

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:45.290
There.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:47.500
What?!

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.390
His butt?!

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:54.920
Yeah!

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:04.410
I accidentally used my... Wait, what?!

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:06.060
What <i>was </i>that?!

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:08.080
He scored a goal with his rump!

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:09.420
Seriously? No way!

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:13.100
I've never seen such godly buttock skills!

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:16.840
Just how I planned it!

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:20.100
That's what the great Tsukamoto Jin can do!

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:21.570
Phew!

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:25.520
You bastard, stealing the spotlight!

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:28.030
You made us worry, you little turd.

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:28.990
Bam.

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:30.190
You did it!

00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:31.060
Bam.

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:33.150
Bam. Bam.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:34.920
I-I can't breathe...

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:36.980
Hey!

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:41.180
Don't get ahead of yourselves!
You only equalized!

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:49.430
In the end, it was an easy victory
for Fujimi High School.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:54.390
<b>Fujimi</b>

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:54.390
<b>1st</b>

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:54.390
<b>2nd</b>

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:54.390
<b>Total</b>

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:54.390
<b>Minamida Fuzoku</b>

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:53.230
After drawing level,
they got two more goals to seal it.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:21:05.550
You were amazing again today! Good work!

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:57.010
Aoyama really is a cut above.

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:08.320
In the final minutes,
Minamida Fuzoku couldn't contain Aoyama.

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:13.690
His team may have won,
but Aoyama was really terrible today.

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:20.460
Aoyama might have played for
that shot by the number 4.

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:25.440
In order to restore his confidence 
after he'd made so many mistakes.

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.220
Victory dance!

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:31.340
If he loses in a place like this,
he'd be throwing his entire career away.

00:21:31.340 --> 00:21:36.640
If he really risked that much 
just to make that one play,

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:39.980
he's an idiot of epic proportions.

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:16.510
<i>It is </i>Weekly Gonz's<i> hugely popular manga,</i>

00:23:16.510 --> 00:23:18.160
<i>with over 10 million volumes in print!</i>

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:22.630
<i>And now, "I'm Going to Save This World"
 is getting an anime adaptation!</i>

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.530
Guess I'll base my new character on him.

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>Ozaki-kun Has His Pride</b>
